(7766677, 1288090, 30861, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by GolferDDS:</b></div><hr/><i> Well done Anita. Those low scores are disgraceful! </i></td></tr></table> Those are probably DNMC scores. I for one felt this didn''t meet the spirit of the challenge. </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>I''m with Posthumous on this. Mine was one of the low scores. For me the spirit of "shoot from the hip" is sort of a "flawed spontaneity" and this shot''s too perfect to qualify even assuming Anita was running backward, holding the camera low, and using no viewfinder. It''s clearly an "intentional" shot in that sense.</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: Originally posted by GolferDDS: Well done Anita. Those low scores are disgraceful!  Those are probably DNMC scores. I for one felt this didn''t meet the spirit of the challenge. 
I''m with Posthumous on this. Mine was one of the low scores. For me the spirit of "shoot from the hip" is sort of a "flawed spontaneity" and this shot''s too perfect to qualify even assuming Anita was running backward, holding the camera low, and using no viewfinder. It''s clearly an "intentional" shot in that sense.', '2024-05-29 09:20:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(7766707, 1288090, 138630, '<td valign="top">
<table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bear_Music:</b></div><hr/><i> . . . 
<br/>I''m with Posthumous on this. Mine was one of the low scores. For me the spirit of "shoot from the hip" is sort of a "flawed spontaneity" and this shot''s too perfect to qualify even assuming Anita was running backward, holding the camera low, and using no viewfinder. It''s clearly an "intentional" shot in that sense. </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>Sorry to admit that I did not vote on this challenge :( - but I would have struggled to find a "fair" score for the same reasons.  The struggle would, of course, have been because it''s a delightful, beautiful, fresh, capture.  As such, I would not have given it below a 5 and would probably have settled on a 6; personally, that''s what I do for wonderful photos that I feel don''t meet the specific challenge.  But I would have reserved my 7-10 scores for something else.</td>', 'Originally posted by Bear_Music: . . . 
I''m with Posthumous on this. Mine was one of the low scores. For me the spirit of "shoot from the hip" is sort of a "flawed spontaneity" and this shot''s too perfect to qualify even assuming Anita was running backward, holding the camera low, and using no viewfinder. It''s clearly an "intentional" shot in that sense. 

Sorry to admit that I did not vote on this challenge :( - but I would have struggled to find a "fair" score for the same reasons.  The struggle would, of course, have been because it''s a delightful, beautiful, fresh, capture.  As such, I would not have given it below a 5 and would probably have settled on a 6; personally, that''s what I do for wonderful photos that I feel don''t meet the specific challenge.  But I would have reserved my 7-10 scores for something else.', '2024-05-29 14:38:26.000000', NULL, 0);
